.\" man/man3/Docv::Term::Decoder.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Term::Decoder" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Term::Decoder \- Decodes terminal input bytes into raw events: kitty \fB\%CSI \%u\fR keys and their legacy letter/tilde forms, plain UTF\-8 and control bytes, SGR mouse reports, terminal notifications and OSC 21 color reports.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Term::Decoder\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Decodes terminal input bytes into raw events: kitty \fB\%CSI \%u\fR keys and
their legacy letter/tilde forms, plain UTF\-8 and control bytes, SGR
mouse reports, terminal notifications and OSC 21 color reports.
Incomplete sequences wait for more bytes; \fB\%flush\fR resolves them (a lone
ESC is the Escape key, an unterminated \fB\%ESC \%]\fR is Alt\-]).
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBMAX_OSC = 8192\fR
Longest operating system command (\fB\%ESC \%] \%... \%ST\fR) accepted.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_SEQUENCE = 512\fR
Longest control sequence accepted before it is discarded.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef feed(bytes : Bytes, & : Event \-> ) : Nil\fR
Decodes \fIbytes\fR, yielding every complete event.
.TP 4
\fBdef flush : Nil\fR
Resolves buffered bytes after an input timeout.
.TP 4
\fBdef pending? : Bool\fR
True when bytes of an incomplete sequence are buffered.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/term/decoder.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::Term" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
